4. Database schema (must have)
Add (or ensure) these columns on the shop session/token table (this app uses sessions):

Column	Type	Purpose
session_id	string	Prefer Shopify offline id: offline_{shop}.myshopify.com
shop	string	example.myshopify.com
access_token	text/string	Current Admin API token
refresh_token	text (not string(255) — tokens can be long)	Current refresh token
expires_at	datetime/nullable	When access_token expires
refresh_token_expires_at	datetime/nullable	When refresh_token expires
scope	string/nullable	Granted scopes
is_online	bool	Offline sessions should be false
Migration checklist for another project
Schema::table('sessions', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->text('refresh_token')->nullable()->after('access_token');
    $table->timestamp('refresh_token_expires_at')->nullable()->after('refresh_token');
    // expires_at may already exist from older Shopify templates
});
Persistence formula

expires_at = now() + expires_in seconds
refresh_token_expires_at = now() + refresh_token_expires_in seconds
5. Config (production-safe)
Do not call env('SHOPIFY_API_KEY') from controllers/services when config is cached.

In config/shopify.php (or equivalent):

return [
    'api_key' => env('SHOPIFY_API_KEY', 'not_defined'),
    'api_secret' => env('SHOPIFY_API_SECRET', 'not_defined'),
    'scopes' => env('SCOPES', 'not_defined'),
    'host' => str_replace('https://', '', env('HOST', 'not_defined')),
    'api_version' => env('SHOPIFY_API_VERSION'),
];
Everywhere else use:

config('shopify.api_key');
config('shopify.api_secret');
Initialize Shopify Context from the same config values in the app service provider.

6. Acquiring expiring tokens
6.1 OAuth authorization code grant (install / reauth)
When: Merchant installs app or is sent through /api/auth.

Where in this project: ExpiringOfflineOAuth::exchangeAuthorizationCode() and persistSession().

Request

POST https://{shop}.myshopify.com/admin/oauth/access_token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=...
client_secret=...
code={authorization_code}
expiring=1
Important

Shopify PHP SDK OAuth::callback() historically exchanges without expiring=1. This project therefore performs the exchange manually and passes expiring=1.
If the expiring exchange fails, you may temporarily fall back to non-expiring for older apps — but public apps must migrate fully before Jan 1, 2027.
Persist all of

access_token
refresh_token
expires_at
refresh_token_expires_at
scope
session_id = offline_{shop}
is_online = false
6.2 Token exchange (merchant has App Bridge session JWT)
When: Embedded app is open; you have Authorization: Bearer <session_token>; offline token is missing/invalid and refresh failed or is unavailable.

Where in this project: TokenExchange::exchange($shop, $sessionToken).

Request

POST https://{shop}.myshopify.com/admin/oauth/access_token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=...
client_secret=...
grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange
subject_token={session_jwt}
subject_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:id_token
requested_token_type=urn:shopify:params:oauth:token-type:offline-access-token
expiring=1
Also used for migration of an existing non-expiring offline token → expiring offline token:

subject_token = {old_non_expiring_offline_access_token}
subject_token_type = urn:shopify:params:oauth:token-type:offline-access-token
requested_token_type = urn:shopify:params:oauth:token-type:offline-access-token
expiring=1
That migration is irreversible for that shop (old non-expiring token is revoked).

7. Refreshing tokens (the heart of the fix)
7.1 Refresh API
Where in this project: TokenExchange::refresh($shop).

Request

POST https://{shop}.myshopify.com/admin/oauth/access_token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=...
client_secret=...
grant_type=refresh_token
refresh_token={stored_refresh_token}
Response (example)

{
  "access_token": "shpat_...",
  "expires_in": 3600,
  "refresh_token": "shprt_...",
  "refresh_token_expires_in": 7776000,
  "scope": "read_products,write_products"
}
7.2 When to refresh
Implemented in TokenExchange::needsRefresh():

Refresh when all are true:

Session has access_token
expires_at is set (expiring token)
refresh_token exists
refresh_token_expires_at is empty or still in the future
Now is at/after (expires_at - REFRESH_BUFFER)
This project uses 300 seconds (5 minutes) buffer so tokens are refreshed before hard expiry
Do not refresh when:

expires_at is null → treat as legacy non-expiring token
no refresh_token → cannot refresh; need exchange/OAuth
refresh_token_expires_at is past → merchant must reopen app
7.3 Concurrency / race safety
Multiple jobs or HTTP requests can refresh at the same time. Shopify invalidates the previous refresh token after use, so double-refresh can brick the shop until reauth.

Required pattern (this project):

$lock = Cache::lock("shopify_token_refresh_{$shop}", 20);
return $lock->block(15, function () use ($shop) {
    // Re-load session inside the lock
    // Re-check needsRefresh() — another worker may have refreshed already
    // Then call Shopify refresh endpoint
    // Persist new tokens
});
If lock times out, re-read DB and use whatever token is there (another process likely refreshed).

7.4 ensureFreshAccessToken (single entrypoint)
Where: TokenExchange::ensureFreshAccessToken(?Session $session): ?Session

Contract for every caller (HTTP, job, webhook, mail, GraphQL helper):

$session = TokenExchange::ensureFreshAccessToken($session);
// now $session->access_token is safe to use (or refresh failed / impossible)
Responsibilities:

Resolve the preferred offline session row (offline_{shop} first)
If needs refresh → call refresh()
Return the up-to-date session model
This must be called before every Admin API usage path, or wrapped in your API client factory (recommended).

8. HTTP request path (embedded admin app)
8.1 Middleware: EnsureShopifySession (shopify.auth)
Where: web/app/Http/Middleware/EnsureShopifySession.php
Applied to: protected groups in web/routes/api.php

Order of operations:

Load current Shopify SDK session (offline).
Resolve shop from query / session / Bearer JWT dest.
Proactive refresh via TokenExchange::ensureFreshAccessToken.
If session locally valid → optional live GraphQL shop { name } probe.
If still not usable:
Try TokenExchange::refresh($shop) again / fall back to DB offline session
If merchant Bearer JWT present → TokenExchange::exchange($shop, $jwt)
If all fail → TopLevelRedirection to /api/auth?shop=... (401 + reauthorize headers for App Bridge).
Do not set proceed = true on every exception during the probe. Auth errors (invalid api key, 401, unauthorized) must force refresh/reauth.

8.2 Helper methods used by controllers
Where: HelperController

getShop($request)
Resolves shop in this order:

shopifySession from middleware attributes
?shop= query
Bearer session JWT dest host
Offline session row via TokenExchange::resolveOfflineSession($shop)
Returns ensureFreshAccessToken($session)
getShopApi($shop_name)
Resolve offline session
ensureFreshAccessToken
Build API client with fresh access_token
Use config('shopify.*') for key/secret/version
Recommendation for other projects: make one API client factory (like getShopApi) and force all Admin API traffic through it so refresh cannot be skipped.

8.3 Direct new Graphql($shop, $token) calls
If any code constructs GraphQL/REST clients manually, it must refresh first:

$session = \App\Lib\TokenExchange::ensureFreshAccessToken($session);
$client = new \Shopify\Clients\Graphql($session->shop, $session->access_token);
This project does that in:

ShopifyFunctionController
ProductController / CustomerController / ShopifyFlowController / parts of HelperController
9. Background jobs
Jobs often run after the access token has already expired. Merchant JWT is not available.

Pattern used here

public function handle()
{
    $this->session = \App\Lib\TokenExchange::ensureFreshAccessToken($this->session);
    // ... Admin API work
}
Or when jobs store only shop domain:

$session = \App\Lib\TokenExchange::ensureFreshAccessToken(
    \App\Lib\TokenExchange::resolveOfflineSession($shop)
);
