10. Webhooks
Webhook handlers typically load the shop by X-Shopify-Shop-Domain.

Pattern

$shop_name = $request->header('x-shopify-shop-domain');
$session = \App\Lib\TokenExchange::ensureFreshAccessToken(
    \App\Lib\TokenExchange::resolveOfflineSession($shop_name)
        ?: Session::where('shop', $shop_name)->first()
);
If the webhook only writes the incoming payload to your DB and does not call Admin API, refresh is optional. If it calls Admin API (metafields, order fetch, etc.), refresh is mandatory.

Webhooks must remain outside shopify.auth middleware (Shopify cannot send App Bridge JWTs).

11. Session identity
Prefer one canonical offline row per shop:

session_id = "offline_" . $shop   // e.g. offline_store.myshopify.com
is_online  = false
TokenExchange::resolveOfflineSession($shop):

Try session_id = offline_{shop}
Else latest row for that shop with non-null access_token
Avoid mixing online user sessions with offline token storage when refreshing.

12. End-to-end sequence diagrams
A) Merchant opens embedded app and calls your API
Frontend (App Bridge)
  → Authorization: Bearer <session_jwt>
  → POST /api/save-option-set

shopify.auth middleware
  → ensureFreshAccessToken (refresh if needed)
  → optionally probe shop { name }
  → if broken: refresh → else exchange(session_jwt)
  → attach shopifySession

Controller
  → HelperController::getShop($request)   // also ensure-fresh
  → HelperController::getShopApi($shop)   // also ensure-fresh
  → Admin GraphQL/REST with fresh token
B) Queue job hours later
Job::handle()
  → ensureFreshAccessToken(session)
      → needsRefresh? yes
      → Cache lock
      → POST grant_type=refresh_token
      → persist new access_token + refresh_token
  → Admin API calls succeed
C) Refresh token itself expired (90 days idle)
ensureFreshAccessToken / refresh
  → refresh_token_expires_at in the past OR Shopify returns invalid refresh
  → cannot recover in background
  → next merchant visit:
       exchange(session_jwt) OR /api/auth OAuth
  → new expiring offline token pair stored
